What this does in plain English

This code:

1. Starts at a possible threshold.
2. Applies the threshold month by month.
3. Suppresses accounts that already evented in the last 3 months.
4. Counts only the newly evented accounts.
5. Checks the average monthly count after month 1.
6. If too many accounts event, it raises the threshold.
7. If too few accounts event, it lowers the threshold.
8. Stops when the monthly average lands around 3.6K–4.4K.

This is the dynamic/cooldown framework aligned to the 80% utilization rule.




